\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Tracing a loop or inserting its field ends}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [Polyakov trace](fdip-00X4) closes a transport
by tracing it. A [dressed pair](fdip-00WD) instead
contracts the transported field with the independent
barred field. On the one-vertex torus, the positive first
loop starts and ends at the same vertex, but these are
still two different operations. Which inverse block
enters the field contraction, and how do its normalized
value and the loop trace differ at mass #{5}?}
